# SD
1. Call Center Staff is a physical and systemic object.
2. Customer is a physical and environmental object.
3. Head Of Development is a physical and systemic object.
4. Marketing Staff is a physical and systemic object.
5. Pre-sales Employee is a physical and systemic object.
6. Sales Representative is a physical and systemic object.
7. Customer Contact is an informatical and systemic object.
8. Customer Contact can be interested, new or uninterested.
9. State new is initial.
10. Customer Response is an informatical and environmental object.
11. Presentation is an informatical and systemic object.
12. Quotation is an informatical and systemic object.
13. Customer Acquiring is an informatical and systemic process.
14. Call Center Staff, Customer, Head Of Development, Marketing Staff, Pre-sales Employee, and Sales Representative handle Customer Acquiring.
15. Customer Acquiring yields Customer Contact, Customer Response, Presentation, and Quotation.
# SD1
1. Customer Acquiring from SD zooms in SD1 into Contact Determining, Customer Calling, Personal Acquiring, Online Presenting, Customer Responding, Follow-up Calling, and Quotation Creating, which occur in that time sequence.
2. Marketing Staff is a physical and systemic object.
3. Customer Contact is an informatical and systemic object.
4. Customer Contact can be interested, new or uninterested.
5. State new is initial.
6. Call Center Staff is a physical and systemic object.
7. Budget of Customer Contact is an informatical and systemic object.
8. Budget of Customer Contact can be huge or normal.
9. Contact Person of Customer Contact is an informatical and systemic object.
10. Head Of Development is a physical and systemic object.
11. Pre-sales Employee is a physical and systemic object.
12. Sales Representative is a physical and systemic object.
13. Presentation is an informatical and systemic object.
14. Customer is a physical and environmental object.
15. Customer Response is an informatical and environmental object.
16. Quotation is an informatical and systemic object.
17. Customer Contact exhibits Budget and Contact Person.
18. Customer Acquiring is an informatical and systemic process.
19. Contact Determining is an informatical and systemic process.
20. Marketing Staff handles Contact Determining.
21. Contact Determining yields Customer Contact.
22. Customer Calling is an informatical and systemic process.
23. Call Center Staff handles Customer Calling.
24. Customer Calling affects Budget of Customer Contact and Contact Person of Customer Contact.
25. Personal Acquiring is an informatical and systemic process.
26. Personal Acquiring occurs if Customer Contact is uninterested, in which case Personal Acquiring changes Customer Contact from uninterested to interested, otherwise Personal Acquiring is skipped.
27. Head Of Development handles Personal Acquiring.
28. Personal Acquiring occurs if Budget of Customer Contact is at state huge, otherwise Personal Acquiring is skipped.
29. Online Presenting is an informatical and systemic process.
30. Pre-sales Employee and Sales Representative handle Online Presenting.
31. Online Presenting occurs if Customer Contact is at state interested, otherwise Online Presenting is skipped.
32. Online Presenting yields Presentation.
33. Customer Responding is an informatical and systemic process.
34. The maximal duration of Customer Responding is 2 week.
35. Customer handles Customer Responding.
36. Customer Responding yields Customer Response.
37. Follow-up Calling is an informatical and systemic process.
38. Sales Representative handles Follow-up Calling.
39. Follow-up Calling yields Customer Response.
40. Follow-up Calling occurs if Customer Responding lasts more than 2 week.
41. Quotation Creating is an informatical and systemic process.
42. Quotation Creating requires Customer Contact.
43. Quotation Creating yields Quotation.
44. Customer Calling changes Customer Contact from new to exactly one of interested or uninterested.
